# Keep graphify to the actual CODE of the chess app.
#
# Why this file matters: graphify reads code structurally (free, no AI), but it
# reads images, PDFs and prose with an AI — which costs real tokens. This folder
# has 233 images and 5.1 MB of puzzle data. Without this file, mapping the app
# would cost far more than it saves, which is the opposite of the point.
#
# After this, graphify sees ~7 real code files instead of 296 files.

# --- Images: 233 of them. Vision extraction is the single most expensive thing
# --- graphify can do, and none of this art tells it anything about the code.
*.png
*.svg
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.ico
icons/
streaks/
avatars/
pieces/
pieces2/

# --- Puzzle content: 11 files, 5.1 MB of pure data. Not architecture.
puzzles/

# --- Third-party libraries. Not my code, and stockfish is a 6.9 MB binary.
vendor/
*.wasm

# --- Data-as-JavaScript. These are big content arrays, not logic. Excluding
# --- them keeps the map about how the app actually works.
js/endgames-data.js
js/quotes-data.js
js/legal-data.js
js/openings-eco.js
js/learning-data.js
js/i18n.js

# --- Graphify's own output. Never map the map.
graphify-out/

# --- My notes TO Claude, not part of the app. The 2026-08-05 run indexed these
# --- and produced junk edges like "Token Rules For Session -> Endgame Tab".
HANDOVER.md
WORK-ORDER.md
READ-TAB-PROMPT.md
DESIGN-AUDIT-PROMPT.md

# --- Build and tooling noise
node_modules/
android/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks
